  "id": "nsw_planning_doc_026",
  "text": "Planning Document: Marrickville DCP 2011 - 9 1 Lewisham North Precinct 1\n\nClause 9.1.2 - heritage (development_control): To protect and preserve the identified period buildings within the precinct and encourage their sympathetic alteration or restoration.\n\nClause 9.1.2 - heritage (development_control): To protect the identified heritage items within the precinct.\n\nClause 9.1.2 - height_limit (development_control): To maintain distinctly single storey streetscapes that exist within the precinct.\n\nClause 9.1.2 - heritage (development_control): To protect significant streetscapes and/or public domain elements within the precinct including landscaping, fencing, open space, sandstone kerbing and guttering, views and vistas and prevailing subdivision patterns.\n\nClause 9.1.2 - environmental_protection (development_control): To ensure that new development considers all potential impacts to biodiversity.\n\nClause 9.1.2 - zoning (development_control): To preserve the predominantly low density residential character of the precinct.\n\nClause 9.1.2 - parking (development_control): To ensure that the provision and location of off-street car parking does not adversely impact the amenity of the precinct.\n\nClause 9.1.4 - other (development_control): New development should address the GreenWay Corridor, recognising the space as an active frontage with substantial visual and environmental benefits; as well as an active transport corridor, and provide opportunities for street activation and/or public art and animation.\n\n",
  "metadata": {
    "document_name": "Marrickville DCP 2011 - 9 1 Lewisham North Precinct 1",
    "extractions_count": 10
